<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Slavonia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Slavonia is a historical region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drava">Drava</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osijek">Osijek</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> the name covered the lands between the Drava and Sava ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> through a ban, and most of it fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the 16th century. Recovered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1699, it was joined with Croatia in 1868 as the Kingdom of Croatia-Slavonia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/slavonia.jpg" alt="Slavonia" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomobe03 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slavonia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
